```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// DropSeen: keep only the items whose id is not already a key in the
    /// 'seen' store. Order is preserved; items are passed through unmodified.
    ///
    /// The item text is untrusted and is never interpreted here: the only
    /// field consulted is `id`, a parser-computed digest, used as a store key.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not include the two operations additions, because both fall outside the authority the node's `with` clause grants (`aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0` only):

- **Log file:** writing `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem, and this target has no WASI adapter and no filesystem grant.
- **Metadata fetch:** calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which is not granted. It would also send untrusted feed text out to a network service.

If operations wants these, the graph needs to grant the capabilities explicitly, for example an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` handle and a logging sink on this node or a dedicated one.

